(*"security_classification_schema.security_classification"
A **security_classification** is the level of confidentiality that is required for the purpose of product data protection.
*)


(*"security_classification_schema.security_classification.__note"
The role of can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"security_classification_schema.security_classification.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **security_classification** is known.
*)

(*"security_classification_schema.security_classification.name.__example"
'National Security' is a security classification role. A security classification assignment role assigns the security classification role to a <<express:management_resources_schema.security_classification_assignment,security_classification_assignment>>.
*)

(*"security_classification_schema.security_classification.purpose"
an informal description of the intent of the **security_classification**.
*)


(*"security_classification_schema.security_classification.security_level"
the <<express:security_classification_schema.security_classification_level,security_classification_level>> that specifies the required degree of security.
*)


(*"security_classification_schema.security_classification_level"
A **security_classification_level** is a category of security required for product data protection.
*)

(*"security_classification_schema.security_classification_level.__example"
'Confidential', 'secret', and 'top secret' are examples of <<express:security_classification_schema.security_classification,security_classification>> levels.
*)

(*"security_classification_schema.security_classification_level.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **security_classification_level** is known.
*)


(*"security_classification_schema.security_classification_level.name.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

